{
 "thread": "p9g7CM2sLoE",
 "subject": "Calculating probabilities of detection for subsets of the population based upon MCDS models",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2014-07-08T17:04:40Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "g1PNvUUxrEsJ",
   "from": "Caloo Ecological Services",
   "author": "e0eb2ff92f74062f",
   "date": "2014-07-07T16:33:24Z",
   "subject": "Calculating probabilities of detection for subsets of the population based upon MCDS models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Dear all, <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">I want to report average probabilities of detection for\r\ndifferent subsets of the population based upon MCDS models, and can see two\r\ndifferent approaches, which yield different results, and I’m trying to\r\nchoose between them. <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">First just calculate the mean of the fitted p values for\r\nthat subset of the population:<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&gt;ddf.result&lt;-ddf(method=ddf.method,dsmodel=dsmodel,data=ddf.dat, \r\nmeta.data=ddf.meta.data)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">&gt; average.p</span></font><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&lt;- mean(ddf.result$fitted[selected])\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">When all data are selected, this gives the same\r\nresult as:<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&gt; mean(ddf.result$fitted)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">[1] 0.5348632<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">My models assume clusters are independently detected,and\r\ncluster size is one of the covariates. Using this approach, I calculate\r\nprobabilities of detection for individuals rather than clusters by weighting\r\neach cluster by its size when calcluating the mean. </span></font><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Second (derived from the code for mrds:::plot.ds),  fit\r\na detection function model for that subset of the population, and calculate the\r\naverage.p values accordingly<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">    </span></font><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">pdot\r\n&lt;- ddf.result$fitted[selected]<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  inverse.pdot.sum&lt;-sum(1/pdot)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  ddfobj &lt;- ddf.result$ds$aux$ddfobj<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  m&lt;- nrow(ddfobj$xmat[selected, ])<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  n&lt;-length(distance)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  p&lt;-rep(0,n)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  for (i in 1:n)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  {<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">    x&lt;-rep(distance[i],m)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">    detfct.values &lt;-\r\nmrds:::detfct(x, ddfobj,select = selected, width = width)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">    p[i]&lt;-sum(detfct.values/pdot)/inverse.pdot.sum<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  }<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">  average.p &lt;-mean(p)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">When all data are selected this gives the same result as:<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&gt; summary(ddf.result)$average.p<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">[1] 0.4890873<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">This approach yields estimates of the average probabilities\r\nof detection for each subset of the population which correspond to the fitted\r\ncurves returned by mrds:::plot.ds. <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">I don’t see how to calculate probabilities of\r\ndetection for individuals using this approach. <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">The two approaches give similar, but different answers, and I’m\r\njust wandering exactly what the differences represent, and if one approach is\r\nto be preferred over the other. <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Thanks for any help<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Nigel <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Dr Nigel Harding<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Caloo Ecological Services<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Unit 8<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Stromness Business Centre<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Back Road<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Stromness<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">Orkney<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">KW16 3AW<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">T: 01856 852814<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial\">M: 07980 479261<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"> </span><u></u><u></u></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<br>\nE-Mail scanned for viruses by The Co-operative Phone &amp; Broadband.\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "xmroId6SfRUJ",
   "from": "Caloo Ecological Services",
   "author": "e0eb2ff92f74062f",
   "date": "2014-07-08T17:04:40Z",
   "subject": "RE: [distance-sampling] Calculating probabilities of detection for subsets of the population based upon MCDS models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<u></u>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">Sorry, I’ve\r\njust realized I’m talking nonsense, and wasting people’s time. Just\r\nin case I’ve have sown unnecessary confusion:<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">Overall Probability\r\nof detection given by number of animals seen, divided by the estimated nos\r\npresent.<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">&gt;\r\nlength(ddf.result$fitted)/sum(1/ddf.result$fitted)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">[1] 0.4890873<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">The same answer\r\nas given by mrds <u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">summary(ddf.result)$average.p<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">[1] 0.4890873<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">And not the same\r\nanswer as is obtained by taking a simple mean of the fitted values.<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">&gt;\r\nmean(ddf.result$fitted)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">[1] 0.5348632<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">To get\r\nprobability of detection for individuals rather than objects:<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">sum(ddf.result$data$size)/sum(ddf.result$data$size/ddf.result$fitted)<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">[1] 0.6286722<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">Best wishes <u></u><u></u></span></font></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:navy\">Nigel<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Dr Nigel Harding<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Caloo Ecological Services<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Unit 8<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Stromness Business Centre<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Back Road<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Stromness<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">Orkney<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">KW16 3AW<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">T: 01856 852814<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial;color:navy\">M: 07980 479261<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"3\" color=\"navy\" face=\"Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:navy\"> </span></font><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
